{"name":"Samantha’s Room","hex":"#f2d7e6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"room","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An opportunity or scope (to do something). .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Space for something, or to carry out an activity."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To reside, especially as a boarder or tenant.","To assign to a room; to allocate a room to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/room"}],"entries":[{"title":"Room","blocks":[{"text":"In a building or a ship, a room is any enclosed space within a structure, typically bounded by walls to which entry is possible only via a door or other dividing structure. The entrance connects it to either a passageway, another room, or the outdoors. The space is typically large enough for several people to move about. The size, fixtures, furnishings, and sometimes placement of the room within the building or ship support the activity to be conducted in it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Ateneul_Rom%C3%A2n_-_Sala.jpg/330px-Ateneul_Rom%C3%A2n_-_Sala.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Room"},{"title":"Samantha","blocks":[{"text":"Samantha is an English feminine given name in use since the 17th century that is of uncertain derivation. It is now in popular use worldwide due to various popular culture influences."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Elizabeth_Montgomery_Bewitched_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Elizabeth_Montgomery_Bewitched_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samantha"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Salle_des_catalogues_de_la_Bibliotheque_Mazarine_Paris.jpg/500px-Salle_des_catalogues_de_la_Bibliotheque_Mazarine_Paris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u